    ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    BOSS 4.2 Update                                                September 19, 2000
    ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Conformational search has been enhanced. If MC conformational search is requested
    and no conformational search specifications are in the Z-matrix, the program will
    select the key non-ring bonds for torsional variation. With the xCS100 and xCS200
    scripts, the resulting conformers are in the plt.mol file. Execution of QikProp on
    plt.mol will then generate the QikProp predictions for each conformer. The
    conformational search and QikProp results can then be combined with the xQPCON
    script to obtain confromationally averaged properties for the gas-phase or
    aqueous-phase conformer distributions. E.g.,
    xCS100 celeco
    xQPROP plt.mol
    xQPCON
    will provide the results for celeco.z (celecoxib) in the drugs directory.

    The key point is that you can perform a reasonable conformational search now without
    providing any conformational search information in the Z-matrix. New scripts
    have also been added -

    xCS100      - execute MC conformational search with 100 starting structures
    xCS200      - execute MC conformational search with 200 starting structures
    xCS100F     - execute MC CS with 100 starting structures - with high resolution
    xCS200F     - execute MC CS with 200 starting structures - with high resolution
    xSS100      - execute stochastic conformational search with 100 starting structures
    xSS200      - execute stochastic conformational search with 200 starting structures
    xSS100F     - execute stochastic CS with 100 starting structures - with high resolution
    xSS200F     - execute stochastic CS with 200 starting structures - with high resolution

    x??100 and x??200 use less stringent comparison criterion for identifying
    duplicate conformers - appropriate for drug-like molecules.

    x??100F and x??200F provide higher resolution for small molecules; e.g., they
    will distinguish trans and gauche ethanol, x??100 and x??200 will not. All
    scripts will distinguish the four pentane conformers.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    With the new conformational search ability, one could

    2D -> 3D to yield drug.mol file
    xMOLZ  drug         ....  convert drug.mol to BOSS Z-matrix file drug.z
    xCS100 drug         ....  perform conformational search on drug.z -> structures in plt.mol

    rm propsum          ....  start new QikProp propsum file
    xQPROP plt.mol      ....  execute QikProp for every conformer -> propsum
    xQPCON              ....  conformationally average QikProp results -> output in out
